29,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings are sobering. Our allocation is down significantly, and we must now pay for floor space from this same limited pot.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It seems our records are incomplete. Work without fixed appointments simply vanishes from our reports, though a previous call-back trial did reduce readmissions.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've found a worrying trend in nursing vacancies, but interestingly, the midwifery rota currently has some unusual slack.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Oh no! The car park is full by eleven and the shuttle only reaches a few villages. We really can't fit more people on site!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I found that joint clinics often fail when neither department wants the budget line, and outside data agreements take forever to sign.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Kenji, if the site is at capacity, perhaps we should look for programs that operate away from the hospital premises.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, that is logical, but my data shows that if it isn't a fixed appointment, the administration ignores the effort.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, that explains why some of our joint efforts feel so fragile. We must ensure the staffing is stable and agreed upon.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, that's a great idea! If we don't need more parking or rooms, the hospital won't seize up!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, exactly. We must avoid arrangements that rely on outside bodies who might not sign the necessary agreements in a timely manner.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I must warn you, however, that contacts made away from the hospital draw no tariff from the regional health fund.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Shion,,So we face a choice between invisible work that helps patients or visible work that drains our limited physical space.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Midori,,And we cannot ignore the nursing shortage. Any program relying on ward nurses will likely fail or cause burnout.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Kenji,,This is tricky! We need something that doesn't need the car park but also doesn't make the nurses too tired.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"We must also avoid anything requiring complex new data agreements with outside surgeries, as those take over a year to finalize.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
