55,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Looking at the candidates, the Perinatal Support Service seems interesting, but the Day Rehabilitation Unit requires dedicated space we may not afford.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Shion,,"The Home Follow-Up Team mirrors the call-back trial that actually worked, though the Chronic Care Coordination might suffer from the data agreement delays.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Midori,,"The Perinatal Support Service aligns perfectly with the slack in the midwifery rota, making it the most sustainable for our staff.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Kenji,,I love the Home Follow-Up Team! It doesn't need the car park or the shuttle because the nurses go to the patients!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I am wary of the Perinatal service being joint, but the Home Follow-Up Team avoids the complex outside surgery agreements.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the Perinatal service is on-site. @Kenji, the Home Follow-Up Team earns no regional tariff, which worries me given our budget cut.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, is a lack of tariff worse than a program that fails because the car park is full? The Home team is logically superior.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, if we use the midwifery slack for the Perinatal service, we aren't adding new pressure to the exhausted ward nurses.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Kenji,,But the Home team is so much better for the patients! They don't have to struggle with the shuttle!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I agree. The Home Follow-Up Team is a simpler structure that avoids the pitfalls of joint-departmental budget wars.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I suppose the lack of tariff is a price we pay for feasibility. The Home Follow-Up Team is the most realistic.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Shion,,It is the only choice that balances proven patient impact with the physical constraints of the facility.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I can support the Home Follow-Up Team, provided we don't pull from the already vacant ward nursing posts.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Kenji,,Yay! I'm totally voting for the Home Follow-Up Team! It's the best fit for our space!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shizue,,It avoids the long wait for data agreements and the instability of joint clinics. I am in agreement.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I cast my vote for the Home Follow-Up Team.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Shion,,I vote for the Home Follow-Up Team.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Midori,,I vote for the Home Follow-Up Team.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I vote for the Home Follow-Up Team!,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I vote for the Home Follow-Up Team.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
